<h1>What to craft next in MTG Arena, Mardu colors (white, black, red)</h1>
<p class="sub">Standard format, snapshot 2026-07-30. This page reads your live Magic: The Gathering Arena collection and ranks every card you might want to make using a Wildcard. The cards that show up in the most decks rise to the top.</p>

<div class="note">
<strong>One-paragraph explainer.</strong> In MTG Arena you turn extra cards into "Wildcards", then spend a Wildcard to make any card of that rarity. Wildcards are the most precious thing in the game. This dashboard sorts every white, black, or red Standard card by how many of the 55 published Mardu-color Standard decklists in this project's harvest actually run it. The more decks a card fits into, the more value you get per Wildcard. You have <strong>8 rare and 4 mythic Wildcards</strong> right now, so the ranking matters.
</div>


<div class="auditbox">
  <h3>Fact audit, 2026-07-30</h3>
  <p style="margin:0 0 8px">Every row was re-checked against live Scryfall on 2026-07-30, and the deck column was recounted from the source decklists by a script written independently of the one that produced it.</p>
  <ul style="margin:0 0 8px 18px">
    <li><span class="good">188 of 188</span> ranked cards verified: name, set printing, rarity, colour identity, type line and mana value all match Scryfall, and every one is Standard-legal.</li>
    <li><span class="good">188 of 188</span> deck counts reproduced by an independent recount against the same 55 decklists.</li>
    <li><span class="bad">4 stale counts corrected:</span> this box claimed <code>20 of 20</code> cards verified for a table holding 188 rows, the priced count read <code>162 of 166</code> against an actual 184 of 188, the wildcard total read <code>162</code> against an actual 187, and the header was dated June 2026 against a 2026-07-30 snapshot.</li>
    <li><span class="bad">Method note was wrong:</span> it described a colour-identity calculation, which the deck column stopped using on 2026-07-30, and it credited &quot;Untapped decklists&quot;, which this project has never decoded. The Method section at the foot now names the real source.</li>
    <li><span class="bad">Unsourced number removed:</span> the Collection tile read <code>62.6%</code> against a denominator of 17,956 unique cards. That figure traces to no file in this project and matches no Scryfall count (<code>game:arena</code> is 15,947, <code>game:arena legal:standard</code> is 4,702), so the tile now shows only what the live pull returns.</li>
    <li><span class="good">Snapshot is current:</span> the collection is stamped <b>2026-07-31</b>, with <b>8 rare</b> and <b>4 mythic</b> wildcards. Finishing every playset still missing across these 141 rows needs <b>173</b> rare-plus-mythic wildcards (120 rare, 53 mythic), so treat the ranking as a priority order rather than a shopping list.</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin:0"><b>Paper $ column.</b> Market price for <b>one copy</b>, cheapest Scryfall printing, sortable. This is the paper value of the card and it takes no account of your Arena collection, because owning it on Arena does not mean owning it in paper. Only the <b>WC to 4-of</b> column subtracts what you own. Priced <b>184 of 188</b> rows; the four blanks are Godless Shrine, Sacred Foundry, Blood Crypt and Boros Charm.</p>
</div>
