<h2 id="creator-decks">Creator decks culled from YouTube (195)</h2>
<p class="sub">Every Standard deck video harvested from 15 tracked creators, carried over from the
<a href="https://drwu-htmls.vercel.app/mtg-creator-decks" target="_blank" rel="noopener">creator-decks cull</a>.
Each row keeps its video link, its decklist host, and, where the list was actually fetchable, the real paper price
and the wildcards Arena would charge you after subtracting what you already own.
<strong>34 of 195 decks are castable in your white/black/red colors</strong>, and of those only
<strong>3 is an actual three-color Mardu deck</strong>. The rest are smaller slices of the same colors:
3 Mardu W/B/R, 5 Orzhov W/B, 7 Boros W/R, 5 Rakdos B/R, 3 Mono-White, 4 Mono-Black, 7 Mono-Red. The cheapest one with a real list is <strong>Mono Red Sligh in 2026?</strong> (Mono-Red) by CovertGoBlue at $7.52 paper and 8 rare-plus-mythic wildcards.</p>

<div class="note">
<strong>"Mardu" means the full W/B/R three-color build, nothing less.</strong> A mono-white deck is a mono-white deck.
An Orzhov deck is white-black. A Boros deck is white-red. A Rakdos deck is black-red. Those all happen to run on the
same mana base you already own, so they are worth listing, and the badge on each row names what the deck actually is
rather than filing all seven combinations under one word. The seven color combinations that fit are
W, B, R, W/B, W/R, B/R, and W/B/R.
</div>
<div class="note">
<strong>How this connects to the craft ranking.</strong> The table at the top of this page ranks single cards by how many
of the 25 tracked archetypes they fit. This table is the other direction: whole 60-card lists that real creators
published, scored by what they would cost you to build right now. A deck badged with any of the seven combinations is
buildable from the white/black/red mana base your collection is already deep in.
</div>
